events.description:
**Super PACs are destroying what’s left of American democracy.**

For over a decade, these billionaire-funded mega-PACs have served as legal loopholes, allowing corporations and the ultra-wealthy to pump unlimited, often anonymous money into our elections. They buy influence. They drown out real voters. And they do it all while claiming to be “independent.”

The Abolish Super PACs Act (H.R.2352) is the strongest legislation in Congress to end this abuse once and for all. It:

-   Caps donations to Super PACs at $5,000 per person, per year;
-   Closes the “coordination” loophole that lets candidates and PACs act like one team;
-   Restores electoral integrity by shifting power from billionaires back to the people.

This bill has overwhelming public support. A NYT/CBS poll found that  **78% of Americans across party lines**  support limiting Super PAC money. But Congress still refuses to act.  **Why? Because many of them benefit from the corruption.**

**That ends now.**

**Use this form to send a direct message to your Senators and Representatives demanding they:**

-   Cosponsor H.R.2352;
-   Speak out publicly in favor of abolishing Super PACs;
-   Push for hearings and a vote—no more stalling.

This is a test of who works for us—and who works for their donors. Let’s make the answer clear.

Join us as we call target voters in our 4 priority Congressional Districts to Take Back the House!

We'll be running virtual phone banks 4 days a week through the November election. 

Tuesdays - CD 48 - Flip Red to Blue for Marni von Wilpert;
Wednesdays - CD 45 - Congressman Derek Tran;
Thursdays - CD 13 - Congressman Adam Gray and CD 22 - Randy Villegas;
Sundays - CD 22 - Flip Red to Blue for Randy Villegas

Whether you’re a seasoned phoner or brand new, you’ll be supported every step of the way. We use a dialer call system to make the calls more efficient so you'll need a computer, laptop or tablet and internet access to make the calls.

Bring a friend and be part of the movement shaping the future of our state and our country.  Join us and help Take Back the House!

Come join us to write postcards with Greater Andover Indivisible's friendly community. Our overarching objective is to get progressive candidates into office approve progressive legislation / defeat MAGA legislation wherever possible.  

NOTE! If you want to replenish your supply in between Panera events, you can pick up postcard packets at the Andover Bookstore, the Purple Couch Bookstore in No. Andover, and Brissonte Gifts in No. Reading during their normal business hours.

Available postcard campaigns vary from week to week and by pick-up location. We write cards to key districts around the country to: 
- Provide info about voter registration and encourage people to register; 
- Remind people of upcoming elections and encourage voting by providing important information about when/where/how to vote; 
- Build name recognition for progressive candidates; 
- Inform people about what their MAGA elected officials are doing;
- and more.

Scripts vary but often use top-of-mind issues, like healthcare and cost of living, to attract recipients' attention.

The aim of this campaign is to increase the political participation of disability communities while also engaging candidates and the media on disability issues. ATVFL invites all stakeholders and advocates in the state to collaborate on effective, nonpartisan efforts to:

Address the concerns of people with disabilities;
Eliminate barriers to voting;
Educate people with disabilities about issues and candidates;
Promote turnout of voters with disabilities; and
Engage candidates and the media on disability issues.

